 ><li> <a href="https://learncardano.io/dashboard/" class="dropdown-item">Dashboard</a></li><li> <a href="" class="dropdown-item"></a></li><li> <a href="https://learncardano.io/wp-login.php?action=logout&#038;redirect_to=https%3A%2F%2Flearncardano.io%2Fcourses%2Fstrike-finance-perpetuals-on-cardano%2F&#038;_wpnonce=3cd19664e6" class="dropdown-item">Disconnect</a></li></ul></div> </template></div></div></nav></header><!-- .site-header --><div id="site-content" class="site-content"><div class="container"><div class="content-sidebar row"><main class="content col-sm-12 col-lg-7 py-3 "><article id="post-28928" class="post-28928 sfwd-courses type-sfwd-courses status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry"><div class="entry-wrap"><header class="entry-header"><h1 class="entry-title clearfix">Strike Finance &#8211; Perpetuals on Cardano</h1></header><div class="entry-content"><div class="learndash learndash_post_sfwd-courses user_has_access"  id="learndash_post_28928"><div class="learndash-wrapper learndash-wrapper--course"><div class="learndash-wrapper learndash-wrap learndash-shortcode-wrap learndash-shortcode-wrap-ld_infobar-28928_28928_0"></div><div class="ld-tabs ld-tab-count-1"><div class="ld-tabs-content"><div
 class="ld-tab-content ld-visible"
 id="ld-tab-content-28928"
 ><figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7" data-src="https://learncardano.io/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/strike-finance-perpetuals-cardano-1.jpg" alt="strike finance perpetuals cardano 1" class="wp-image-28992 lazyload" title="Strike Finance - Perpetuals on Cardano 1"><noscript><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1920" height="1080" src="https://learncardano.io/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/strike-finance-perpetuals-cardano-1.jpg" alt="strike finance perpetuals cardano 1" class="wp-image-28992 lazyload" title="Strike Finance - Perpetuals on Cardano 2" srcset="https://learncardano.io/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/strike-finance-perpetuals-cardano-1.jpg 1920w, https://learncardano.io/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/strike-finance-perpetuals-cardano-1-242x136.jpg 242w, https://learncardano.io/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/strike-finance-perpetuals-cardano-1-856x482.jpg 856w, https://learncardano.io/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/strike-finance-perpetuals-cardano-1-768x432.jpg 768w, https://learncardano.io/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/strike-finance-perpetuals-cardano-1-1536x864.jpg 1536w" sizes="(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px" /></noscript></figure><p class="wp-block-paragraph">Strike Finance is a decentralised derivatives protocol built on the Cardano blockchain. It offers a suite of financial instruments, including perpetual futures, options, forwards, and interest rate swaps. Its perpetual futures product allows traders to speculate on asset prices with leverage without expiration, enabling positions to be held indefinitely.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">Perpetual contracts have been a <em>major growth driver</em> in DeFi ecosystems on other blockchains, particularly Ethereum, Arbitrum, and BNB Chain.</p><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Growth Impact of Perpetuals on Other Chains</h2><h3 class="wp-block-heading">1. <strong>Volume and User Activity</strong></h3><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><strong>dYdX (Ethereum → Cosmos)</strong>: At its peak, dYdX saw <strong>daily volumes over $1B</strong>, outpacing many spot DEXs. Its success showcased demand for leveraged, non-custodial trading.<br><a href="https://www.dydx.xyz/annual-report/2024" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Please refer to dYdX&#8217;s 2024 annual report</a>.</li><li><strong>GMX (Arbitrum &amp; Avalanche)</strong>: GMX introduced zero slippage trading via oracle pricing and quickly became the <strong>top dApp on Arbitrum by TVL</strong>, with over <strong>$150M TVL</strong> and strong fee generation.</li><li><strong>Gains Network (Polygon &amp; Arbitrum)</strong>: Focused on synthetic trading with minimal collateral. It demonstrated that users are drawn to leveraged markets even on less congested L2s.</li></ul><h3 class="wp-block-heading">2. <strong>Sticky Liquidity and Fee Generation</strong></h3><ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Perpetuals generate <strong>recurring fees</strong> from:<ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Open/close trades</li><li>Liquidations</li><li>Funding payments (between long/short)</li></ul></li><li>GMX, for instance, regularly generated <span style="box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px;"><strong>$200k-$300k/day in fees</strong>&nbsp;during market volatility, rewarding liquidity providers and token holders. Please refer to the&nbsp;<a href="https://stats.gmx.io/arbitrum" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GMX live analytics</a>&nbsp;for the&nbsp;</span>current total fees generated.</li></ul><h3 class="wp-block-heading">3. <strong>Institutional and Whale Participation</strong></h3><ul class="wp-block-list"><li>Perpetuals are more appealing to experienced traders, whales, and even trading firms looking for leverage without custodial risk.</li><li>Their usage has a <strong>flywheel effect</strong>; more traders, liquidity, fees, and incentive to provide liquidity.</li></ul><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.strikefinance.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Visit their website</a> for more information on Strike Finance or refer to their <a href="https://docs.strikefinance.org/introduction" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">documentation</a> for more detailed information.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">In this course, you will learn about perpetual, how to use Strike Finance, place a long, short, and close your position, along with staking and managing $STRIKE tokens on the platform.</p><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Interview with Shan from Strike Finance</h2><figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper"> <iframe class="lazyload" title="Derivatives Trading, Understanding Options, Forced and Perpetual Trading with Strike Finance" width="1280" height="720" data-src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/FzkDJyDTB3U?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></div></figure></div></div> <!--/.ld-tabs-content--></div> <!--/.ld-tabs--><div class="learndash-wrapper learndash-wrap learndash-shortcode-wrap learndash-shortcode-wrap-course_content-28928_28928_0"><div class="learndash user_has_access" id="learndash_post_28928"><div class="learndash-wrapper"><div class="ld-item-list ld-lesson-list ld-course-content-28928" data-shortcode_instance="{&quot;course_id&quot;:28928,&quot;post_id&quot;:28928,&quot;group_id&quot;:0,&quot;paged&quot;:1,&quot;num&quot;:20,&quot;wrapper&quot;:true,&quot;user_id&quot;:0}"><div class="ld-section-heading"><h2> Course Content</h2><div class="ld-item-list-actions" data-ld-expand-list="true"> <button
